  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: chunk data smuggling in the APNG push-mode reader\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-40930.patch: consume the chunk body and the\n       CRC field in the three inter-frame discard paths of\n       png_push_read_chunk (pngpread.c), so that bytes inside an ignored\n       chunk are no longer reinterpreted as a fresh chunk header on the\n       next png_process_data call, and pass the real chunk length to\n       png_ensure_sequence_number in png_push_read_IDAT (pngpread.c), so\n       that an fdAT chunk shorter than its own sequence number no longer\n       underflows idat_size and swallows the rest of the stream as frame\n       data\n     - CVE-2026-40930",
